From 4d773b9b57cc38a36bd6ded72eb5e11981a39c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:03:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 45/57] drm/gma500: build an SGX545 TA and 3D job for a first
 triangle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add sgx_tri.c, pure builders for every structure of one tiled render: the
HW render context, the parameter buffer descriptor, block and host-built
page table, the RT data set with its zeroed TADATA buffers, the render
details with the 3D registers, and the TA command with the TA registers and
a TA and a 3D status word as completion fences. They follow the layouts and
the minimal job worked out from the closed GLES2 stack's captures and the
microkernel's TA and 3D paths in design/sgx545_3d.md (§4-§8, §12.6, §13).

The scene is one opaque triangle in clip space through a 64x64 viewport,
drawn by the VDM control stream (an MTE state block, an index list with its
vertex task, the end-of-scene block, terminate), with a background object
filling the rest of the ARGB8888 target. Its GPU programs are our own,
assembled from SGXhumation's tools/usse-asm/progs/ into sgx_tri_progs.h: a
vertex fetch and a pass-through vertex shader, the MTE state copies, the
constant-colour pixel shader, and the end-of-tile path of the transfer
queue. sgx_tri.c patches the per-placement fields (DOUTU words, immediates,
PBE words, the next-phase address of the vertex shader).

A CPU reference gives the expected coverage of each pixel, with a pixel of
tolerance at the edges. KUnit checks every field against the documented
offsets and values, the program patches and the reference.

Assisted-by: LLM
